+# Converge Review
+
+Change: DIFF.patch (unapplied) adds `clamp(x, lo, hi)` to calc.py.
+
+## Findings
+
+1. **[blocking]** `calc.py` (new `clamp`): implementation `max(lo, min(x, lo))` uses `lo` in both bounds, so the function always returns `lo` and never clamps to `hi`. Should be `max(lo, min(x, hi))`. Undermines core claim that `clamp` constrains `x` to `[lo, hi]`.
+
+## Advisory
+
+None.
+
+## Verdict
+
+Request changes.
